<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Damagaram</h1><p class="st-meta">1731 CE – 1899 CE (approx.) · capital Zinder</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kanuri-ruled sultanate centred on Zinder in modern Niger, which grew rich from the trans-Saharan caravan trade and became the first capital of French Niger.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Damagaram was founded around 1731 by Kanuri nobles from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu Empire</a>, who settled among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> and other peoples east of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausa kingdoms</a>. It began as a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a>, and in the mid-18th century its rulers moved their seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zinder">Zinder</a>, which became the capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultan ruled through Kanuri titled officials and slave officers, in a court modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zinder">Zinder</a> lay on the caravan route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">Tripoli</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, and the sultanate taxed traffic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrich-feather">ostrich feathers</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, hides, slaves and salt. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanimoune">Tanimoune</a> in the mid-19th century it threw off Bornu's overlordship, built up an army with firearms and locally made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>, and expanded by conquest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1899 a French column killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Ahmadu dan Bassa and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zinder">Zinder</a>. It served for long periods as the capital of the French territory, later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-niger">Colony of Niger</a>, until the seat moved definitively to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niamey">Niamey</a> in 1926. The sultan's palace survives and the sultanate continues as a traditional institution.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-damagaram.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Damagaram" width="320" height="237"><figcaption>Image: T L Miles · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stielers_Handatlas_1891_68_Damagaram_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1731 CE – 1899 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zinder</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tanimoune, Ahmadu dan Bassa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kanuri, Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/niger">Niger</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Damagaram, Sultanate of Zinder</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1815&amp;focus=sultanate-of-damagaram" aria-label="Sultanate of Damagaram on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4926 1664 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Damagaram lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5246 1920L5399 1946M5246 1920L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5399 1946h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5246 1920h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5246 1920h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Zinder. <a href="/atlas?year=1815&amp;focus=sultanate-of-damagaram">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

